[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Backend High Level Requirements
UID: GSSC-BACKEND-HIGH-LEVEL-REQUIREMENTS
VERSION: 5.0.0

[GRAMMAR]
ELEMENTS:
- TAG: TEXT
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
- TAG: SECTION
  PROPERTIES:
    IS_COMPOSITE: True
    PREFIX: None
    VIEW_STYLE: Narrative
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
- TAG: REQUIREMENT
  PROPERTIES:
    PREFIX: GSSC-BHLR-
    VIEW_STYLE: Table
  FIELDS:
  - TITLE: UID
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: TITLE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: STATEMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: RATIONALE
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: COMMENT
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: False
  - TITLE: DERIVED
    TYPE: SingleChoice(True, False)
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: CHANGE_DRIVER
    TYPE: String
    REQUIRED: True
  - TITLE: REVIEW_STATUS
    TYPE: SingleChoice(Changed, Approved, Baselined)
    REQUIRED: True
  RELATIONS:
  - TYPE: Parent
    ROLE: Refines
    REVERSE_ROLE: Refined By

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-SERVICE-TRANSACTIONS
TITLE: Service Transactions

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-USER-ACCOUNTS
TITLE: User Accounts

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-ACCOUNT-ACCESS
TITLE: Account Access

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-1
TITLE: Member Login
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL let a member log in.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Login is how the Unified Backend authenticates a member. The backend uses a retained hash of the member's password. Other keys used for that login are held outside the Unified Backend.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-47
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-2
TITLE: Login Token
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL issue a Login Token when a member login succeeds.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A successful login has to yield a Login Token that a later challenge can test. The Unified Backend PIRs require member authentication and do not require a token.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-3
TITLE: Token Challenge
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL report a challenged Login Token as valid or invalid.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The frontend uses this challenge to detect whether a member is logged in. The report is only valid or invalid. This requirement does not return the contents of the Login Token.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-4
TITLE: Member Logout
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL end the member login of a Login Token when that member logs out.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A member has to be able to end a login. After logout, that Login Token no longer represents a valid login.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-50
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-5
TITLE: Login Token Expiration
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL expire each Login Token.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A Login Token remains valid only for a limited time. This requirement does not set that time.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-179
TITLE: Login Token Cookie
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL deliver the Login Token in an HTTP cookie.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Login Token reaches the client as an HTTP cookie. Cookie attributes and request handling are in the LLRs. Derived from member authentication: the Unified Backend PIRs require a valid login and do not require a cookie medium.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-182
TITLE: Login Token Retention
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL retain each Login Token across Unified Backend restarts.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A member remains logged in after the Unified Backend restarts until that Login Token expires or the member logs out. Retention is durable storage, not process memory. Derived from member authentication: the Unified Backend PIRs require a valid login and do not require durable Login Token retention.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-33, GSSC5-48
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

