A member account has to include a way to reach the member by phone.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-105
TITLE: Stored Secondary Phone Number
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store a member's Secondary Phone Number.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The member account holds the Secondary Phone Number that the member can view and modify.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-116
TITLE: Stored Secondary Phone Number Display
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store whether a member's Secondary Phone Number is displayed.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The account holds the member's choice to display the Secondary Phone Number when one is provided.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-106
TITLE: Stored Preferred Contact Method
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store a member's Preferred Contact Method.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The member account holds the Preferred Contact Method that the member can view and modify. The allowed values remain Email, Phone, or None.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-ACCOUNT-ADDRESSES
TITLE: Addresses

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-107
TITLE: Stored Home Address
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store a member's Home Address.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The member account holds the Home Address that the member can view and modify. This requirement does not define the parts of an address.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-117
TITLE: Stored Home Address Display
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store whether a member's Home Address is displayed in full or redacted.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The account holds the Home Address display that the member or an administrator can set. Redacted shows the city and state. This requirement does not apply to the Mailing Address.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-108
TITLE: Stored Mailing Address
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store a member's Mailing Address.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The member account holds the Mailing Address that the member can view and modify. This requirement does not define the parts of an address.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-109
TITLE: Stored Account Photo
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store a member's Account Photo.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The member account holds the Account Photo that the member can view and modify. This requirement does not define the form of the photo.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-110
TITLE: Stored Position
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store a member's Position.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The member account holds the Position that the member can view. An administrator can modify any member's Position. A user moderator can modify the Position of another member who is not an administrator. Empty is the default, and a member with an empty Position is left off the leadership list. A populated Position is the member's leadership role. This requirement does not name the positions.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-12
GSSC5-36
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-111
TITLE: Stored Site Privileges
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store a member's Site Privileges.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The member account holds the Site Privileges that an administrator can modify. This requirement does not name the privileges.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-ACCOUNT-PASSWORD
TITLE: Password

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-112
TITLE: Stored Current Password Hash
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store a member's current password hash.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The member account holds a hash of the current password so the password itself is not stored. This requirement does not set the hash method.
<<<
