[[/SECTION]]

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-WEBPAGE-DATA
TITLE: Webpage Data

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-GLOBAL-WEBSITE-DATA
TITLE: Global Website Data

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-119
TITLE: Global Website Data
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store global data for the website in a key-value store.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
This data applies to the website as a whole, rather than to one page. This requirement does not define the keys or the values.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-180
TITLE: Public Key-Value Entry
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL provide the public with a stored key-value entry upon request by key.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A caller without a login can request one entry from the key-value store by key and receive that entry when it is stored. This requirement does not define the keys.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-43
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-181
TITLE: Key-Value Entry Modification
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL accept creation or replacement of a key-value entry by an administrator.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
An administrator keeps global website data current. Creation stores a new key. Replacement updates the value for an existing key. How the administrator is authenticated is low-level.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-43
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-50
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-149
TITLE: Artifact Files
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store artifacts on the server as files.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
These artifacts belong to the website as a whole. They are kept as files on the server. This requirement does not define which artifacts are stored, or the form of those files.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-57
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-154
TITLE: Artifact Publicity Status
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store the publicity status of each stored artifact as public or members-only.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The status records whether that artifact is available to the public or only to members. The artifact is a file stored on the server.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-57
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-160
TITLE: Artifact Modification Permissions
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store the permissions required to modify each stored artifact.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The artifact holds the permissions a logged-in member must have to modify it. These permissions are separate from the permissions that allow deletion. This requirement does not name those permissions.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-57
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-178
TITLE: Artifact Deletion Permissions
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store the permissions required to delete each stored artifact.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The artifact holds the permissions a logged-in member must have to delete it. These permissions are separate from the permissions that allow modification. This requirement does not name those permissions.
<<<
DERIVED: False
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PIR-57
  ROLE: Refines

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-GENERIC-PAGE-DATA
TITLE: Generic Page Data

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-120
TITLE: Page Data Table
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store sections, announcements, and event details as entries in the page data table.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Sections, announcements, and event details share this table. Each entry is one section, one announcement, or one event's details. The cemetery project and the war veterans project have their own datasets.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-124
TITLE: Generic Page Datatype
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store a datatype for each page data table entry.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The datatype records whether the entry is a section, an announcement, or event details. This requirement does not define further datatype values.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-121
TITLE: Generic Page Headers
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store headers for each page data table entry.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A page data table entry holds its headers. This requirement does not set how many headers an entry has.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-122
TITLE: Generic Page Bodies
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store bodies for each page data table entry.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A page data table entry holds its bodies. This requirement does not set how many bodies an entry has.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-123
TITLE: Generic Page Resources
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store resources for each page data table entry.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A page data table entry holds its resources. This requirement does not define what a resource contains, or how many an entry has.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-134
TITLE: Generic Page Audience
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store whether each page data table entry is public or members-only.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The flag records whether the entry is available to the public or only to members.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-185
TITLE: Page Entry Content and Metadata Storage
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store content and metadata for each section, announcement, and event-details page data table entry, including tags and permission-related metadata needed for create, modify, and delete, and template-related metadata when that entry uses a template.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Sections, announcements, and event details share content and metadata storage. Tags support grouping and future page ownership. Templates may apply beyond sections when an entry uses one. Order among entries that share a page uses the unified page-data index requirement. Exact field shapes are low-level.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-37
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-186
TITLE: Page Entry Template Capability
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL provide templates that administrators manage and that logged-in members use when creating page data entries that use templates, including sections and announcements or event details when those entries use templates.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Templates supply category and defaults at creation for entries that use them. Get, list, create, modify, and delete of templates, and which attributes a template holds, are low-level.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-37
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-187
TITLE: Generic Page Index
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store an index for each page data table entry that determines that entry's order among entries that share a page.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Index is shared by sections, announcements, and event details in the page data table. How page sharing is determined and the exact index type are low-level.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-37
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-140
TITLE: Generic Page Modification Permissions
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store the permissions that allow modification of each page data table entry.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The entry holds the permissions a logged-in member must have to modify it. This requirement does not name those permissions.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-BHLR-141
TITLE: Generic Page Deletion Permissions
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Unified Backend SHALL store the permissions that allow deletion of each page data table entry.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The entry holds the permissions a logged-in member must have to delete it. These permissions are separate from the permissions that allow modification. This requirement does not name those permissions, and it does not define the deletion operation.
<<<
DERIVED: True
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-12
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

